TITLE:: PltTrack
summary:: Descriptors over time, as stacked small multiples with onsets marked
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltMap, Classes/Onsets, Classes/SpecCentroid

DESCRIPTION::
The analysis-to-mapping chain made visible: what a descriptor actually does while a
sound plays, next to the others, on one clock, with onsets as ticks through every
panel.

A track given no code::lo:: and code::hi:: autoscales over what is currently
visible, which is usually right for a descriptor whose range nobody remembers.

The time axis reads seconds ago, from code::span.neg:: to 0.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: specs
An Array of Events describing the tracks:
code::
(name: "loudness", lo: 0, hi: 64, unit: "sones", colorKey: \ink)
::
code::lo:: and code::hi:: may be left out, in which case the track autoscales.
argument:: span
Seconds visible.
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: analysis
The built in analysis of one bus: link::Classes/Loudness::,
link::Classes/SpecCentroid::, link::Classes/SpecFlatness:: and
link::Classes/Onsets::. All four are core UGens, so nothing extra has to be
installed.
argument:: bus
argument:: server
argument:: span
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: push
One frame: an Array in track order, or an Event keyed by track name. Values that are
not numbers are skipped rather than drawn.
code::
t.push([2000, 0.3]);
t.push((cutoff: 3000, q: 0.5));
::
argument:: values
argument:: time
Defaults to now. Pass it to place a frame yourself.

METHOD:: mark
An onset, drawn as a tick through every panel.

METHOD:: reset
METHOD:: rangeOf
The visible range of one track: its own if given, otherwise what is on screen.

METHOD:: start
METHOD:: stop
The analysis synth and its responders. Rebuilt through link::Classes/ServerTree::,
so they come back after cmd-period.

METHOD:: tracks
METHOD:: marks
METHOD:: span
METHOD:: rate
Analysis frames per second.
METHOD:: onsetThreshold
Passed to link::Classes/Onsets::.
METHOD:: fftSize
METHOD:: panelGap
METHOD:: maxPoints
METHOD:: bus
METHOD:: server
METHOD:: replyId

EXAMPLES::
code::
// the built in analysis of the output bus
s.boot;
t = PltTrack.analysis(0).front;
x = { Blip.ar(LFNoise0.kr(1).exprange(60, 300), 12, 0.2) ! 2 }.play;
x.free;
x = { WhiteNoise.ar(0.2) ! 2 }.play;        // flat, high centroid
x.free;
t.close;

// tracks of your own, pushed from a pattern
(
t = PltTrack([
	(name: "freq", lo: 100, hi: 1000, unit: "Hz"),
	(name: "amp", lo: 0, hi: 0.5)
], 8, "what the pattern is doing").front;

q = Pbind(
	\dur, Pwhite(0.05, 0.2),
	\freq, Pbrown(120, 900, 80),
	\amp, Pwhite(0.05, 0.4)
).collect { |ev|
	t.push([ev[\freq], ev[\amp]]);
	ev
}.play;
)
q.stop; t.close;

// anything with a number can drive it
(
t = PltTrack([(name: "cpu"), (name: "nodes")], 20, "server load").front;
Routine({ loop { t.push([s.avgCPU, s.numSynths]); 0.2.wait } }).play(AppClock);
)
::
